## Model Scaffolding

Generate complete CRUD scaffolding from config:

```bash
gux model add              # Interactive model builder
gux model add --from-config # Generate from gux.config.json
gux model regen Client     # Regenerate after config changes
```

Define models in `gux.config.json`:

```json
{
  "models": {
    "Client": {
      "sections": {
        "Contact": [
          { "name": "FirstName", "type": "string", "required": true, "table": true },
          { "name": "Email", "type": "string", "input": "email" }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Generated files: `guxgen/models/*_gen.go`, `guxgen/dto/*_gen.go`, `guxgen/admin/*_gen.go`, `admin/hooks_gen.go`

## Admin Page Hooks

Customize generated admin pages without editing generated code. Create hook files in `admin/` (e.g., `admin/order_hooks.go`):

```go
func init() {
    SetOrderDetailActions(func(ctx HookContext, item dto.OrderDetail) []core.Node { ... })
    SetOrderBeforeSave(func(ctx HookContext, data map[string]any, isEdit bool) error { ... })
}
```

Available: `Set{Model}ListActions`, `ListRowActions`, `DetailActions`, `DetailSections`, `FormSections`, `BeforeSave`, `AfterSave`. See the skill file for full signatures.

## Parent-Child Models

Configure child models with `"parent"`, `"parentField"`, and `"sidebar": false` in `gux.config.json`. This generates inline child tables on the parent detail page.

## Audit Logging

Enable automatic audit trailing for CRUD models:

```go
app.CRUD(models.Document{}, core.WithAuditLog())
app.CRUD(models.User{}, core.WithAuditLog("PasswordHash"))
```

View logs: register `app.CRUD(core.AuditEntry{}, core.WithRoles("admin"))` and build an admin page.

## CRUD Filtering

List endpoints accept query params: `GET /__gux_api/crud/orderitems?order_id=2`. Use `api.OrderItems.ListFiltered(params, callback)` in code.

## Development Notes

- **Always use `gux dev`** (not `go run`) - it builds WASM and CSS
- **`gux build` always runs `gux gen` first** - never manually edit `guxgen/` files
- Use `r.OnLoad()` for data fetching (supports SSR hydration)
- DTOs hide sensitive fields from API responses
- Mark cross-bundle links as `External: true`
- Hook files in `admin/` (e.g., `order_hooks.go`) are never overwritten by regeneration

## Generated Files (Do Not Edit)

- `guxgen/` - API client, WASM entry points, models, DTOs, admin pages (layout, dashboard, settings, model CRUD)
- `admin/hooks_gen.go` - Hook setter functions (regenerated, but user hook files are preserved)
- `assets_gen.go` - Embedded assets

Run `gux gen` to regenerate after changing models or routes.

## Customizing Generated Admin Pages

All admin pages live in `guxgen/admin/` and are **regenerated on every `gux gen` or `gux build`**. Do not edit these files directly — changes will be lost.

To customize a generated admin page:

1. **Copy** the file from `guxgen/admin/` to your project's `admin/` directory (e.g., `cp guxgen/admin/dashboard.go admin/dashboard.go`)
2. **Update `app.go`** to import your local `admin` package instead of (or in addition to) `guxgen/admin`, and update route references to point to the local copy
3. Your local copy will not be overwritten by regeneration

**For minor customizations**, prefer using Admin Page Hooks (see above) — hooks survive regeneration without needing to copy files.
